      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98000' id='96' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
            <zone h='98000' id='77' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='82400' x='800' y='1000'>
              <zone h='98000' id='34' type-v2='layout-basic' w='82400' x='800' y='1000'>
                <zone h='6370' id='15' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='82400' x='800' y='1000'>
                  <zone h='6370' id='19' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='82400' x='800' y='1000'>
                    <zone fixed-size='94' h='5370' id='16' is-fixed='true' type-v2='dashboard-object' w='10200' x='1200' y='1500'>
                      <button action='tabdoc:goto-sheet window-id=&quot;{2355E241-6536-4C3D-8F22-B9DFAB85098E}&quot;'>
                        <button-visual-state>
                          <image-path>Image/home_new.png</image-path>
                          <tooltip-text>House image which links to landing page</tooltip-text>
                        </button-visual-state>
                      </button>
                      <zone-style>
                        <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                        <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                        <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                        <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                        <format attr='background-color' value='#2f63a2' />
                      </zone-style>
                    </zone>
                    <zone fixed-size='936' forceUpdate='true' h='5370' id='17' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='68200' x='11400' y='1500'>
                      <formatted-text>
                        <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Arial' fontsize='16'>&lt;Sheet Name&gt;</run>
                      </formatted-text>
                      <zone-style>
                        <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                        <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                        <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                        <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                        <format attr='background-color' value='#2f63a2' />
                      </zone-style>
                    </zone>
                    <zone alt-text='Surrey County Council logo' h='5370' id='18' is-scaled='1' param='Image/surreycc_blue.JPG' type-v2='bitmap' w='3200' x='79600' y='1500'>
                      <zone-style>
                        <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                        <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                        <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                        <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                        <format attr='background-color' value='#2f63a2' />
                      </zone-style>
                    </zone>
                    <zone-style>
                      <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                      <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                      <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                      <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                      <format attr='background-color' value='#2f63a2' />
                    </zone-style>
                  </zone>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='19255' id='30' type-v2='text' w='82400' x='800' y='7370'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontname='Arial'>Climate science deals with many kinds of uncertainty and can&apos;t clearly indicate timescales. Instead, Climate Projections are calculated based on the average measurements over 20 years. When the average temperature over 20 years is above the average temperature between 1850 and 1900 this can be converted from a time period into a measurement of global warming.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontname='Arial'>Warming Scenarios indicate the kinds of weather patterns we could expect to observe at certain warming thresholds. Currently we should prepare for warming scenarios of 2 degrees and assess the risk of 4 degree warming scenarios.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontname='Arial'>The actual warming reached between 2001 and 2020 was 0.87 degrees.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontname='Arial'>Use the visualisation below to assess the impact at different warming thresholds on Surrey</run>
